# Complement image (docs/workstreams/14-test-and-conformance.md, PLAN.md section 12 layer L3).
# Builds the real `hs` binary (crates/hs-cli, `[[bin]] name = "hs"`) -- there has never been a
# crate named `hs-server`; an earlier draft of this file referenced one that never existed. See
# docs/status/14-test-and-conformance.md for the date this was fixed and the run it produced.
#
# `hs serve` does not terminate TLS itself (`crates/hs-cli/src/serve.rs` logs a warning and binds
# plaintext even when a listener's `tls:` block is set -- confirmed by reading that file, not
# assumed). Complement requires HTTPS on 8448 for federation traffic. Rather than wait on another
# track to add TLS termination to `hs serve`, this image runs `stunnel4` (a few hundred KB,
# purpose-built for exactly this: terminate TLS on one port, forward plaintext to another) in
# front of `hs`, which listens on 8008 plaintext for both client and federation resources (the
# same `axum::Router` serves every configured resource regardless of which listener it came in
# on -- see `crate::serve::build_router`'s doc comment -- so one plaintext listener is enough; only
# the *port Complement dials* needs to be HTTPS).
#
# Complement's image contract (refs/complement/README.md's "Image requirements" and "Complement
# PKI" sections), verified against `refs/complement/internal/docker/deployer.go`:
#   - EXPOSE 8008 (plain HTTP client-server + federation-over-plaintext-behind-stunnel) and 8448
#     (HTTPS federation traffic, terminated by stunnel here).
#   - Accept the server name via the `SERVER_NAME` environment variable at container start
#     (`deployer.go:366`, `env = []string{"SERVER_NAME=" + hsName}`).
#   - 200 OK on GET /_matrix/client/versions once healthy.
#   - Trust /complement/ca/ca.crt (copied into the container by Complement itself via
#     `docker cp`-equivalent, not a bind mount -- `deployer.go:467`) and sign this server's own
#     federation TLS certificate against /complement/ca/ca.key at *container start*, not image
#     build time (`startup.sh` does this, following refs/complement/README.md's exact `openssl`
#     recipe).
#   - Use `complement` as the shared secret for Synapse-compatible admin registration
#     (`/_synapse/admin/v1/register`) if that endpoint exists; if it 404s, Complement skips those
#     tests instead of failing (confirmed: `client/auth.go`'s `RegisterSharedSecret` skips on a
#     non-2xx `GET`). This server does not mount that route yet (see
#     docs/status/14-test-and-conformance.md's per-track triage), so Complement will skip
#     shared-secret-registration tests and use normal `m.login.dummy` registration for the rest.
#   - Manage its own storage inside the container (the embedded `hs-kv`/Fjall backend -- exactly
#     PLAN.md section 7's single-binary, embedded-store mode).
#   - Tolerate CMD/ENTRYPOINT being invoked more than once per container lifetime (`startup.sh`'s
#     cert-signing and config-writing steps are idempotent: `if [ ! -f ... ]` guards).
#
# The build context for this file is NOT `.` -- see build.sh, which streams a tar excluding
# `target/` (tens of GB on this workspace) and other large, build-irrelevant directories instead
# of using `.dockerignore` (a root-level file this track does not own).

# ---- build stage -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FROM rust:1.98-slim AS build
WORKDIR /workspace

# pkg-config/libssl-dev: some transitive dependency in this workspace's Cargo.lock may need a
# system OpenSSL at build time even where rustls is preferred elsewhere; cheap to have, expensive
# to discover missing after a 10+ minute build.
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends pkg-config libssl-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY . .

# --jobs 4, not the full core count: this machine is shared with several other agents' `cargo`
# invocations at once (see this track's brief and docs/status/dashboard.md), and a release build
# of the whole dependency graph is the single most CPU-hungry thing this track does.
RUN cargo build --release --jobs 4 -p hs-cli

# ---- runtime stage ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FROM debian:trixie-slim
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    openssl ca-certificates curl stunnel4 \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

COPY --from=build /workspace/target/release/hs /usr/local/bin/hs
COPY tests/complement/startup.sh /startup.sh
COPY tests/complement/stunnel.conf.template /stunnel.conf.template
RUN chmod +x /startup.sh
# Complement's real deployer copies the CA cert/key into this directory via the low-level
# CopyToContainer API, which creates any missing parent directories itself (verified by reading
# refs/complement/internal/docker/deployer.go's `copyToContainer`); this directory is created here
# anyway so a plain `docker cp` (used for local smoke-testing this image without Complement, and
# by any Docker client that doesn't behave the same way) also works.
RUN mkdir -p /complement/ca

# Embedded storage lives at /data, inside the container's own writable layer -- deliberately NOT
# a `VOLUME /data` declaration: Complement's own deployer warns "has a named VOLUME /data -
# volumes can lead to unpredictable behaviour due to test pollution" (confirmed: it printed this
# warning against an earlier build of this image), and an anonymous volume is exactly the kind of
# extra state a from-scratch container for each test should not have.
WORKDIR /data

EXPOSE 8008 8448

HEALTHCHECK --interval=1s --timeout=1s --start-period=30s --retries=30 \
    CMD curl -sf http://localhost:8008/_matrix/client/versions || exit 1

ENTRYPOINT ["/startup.sh"]
